From 6bba77e332a3c28b45233e0ab981812034eaea3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:07:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 52/52] Switch: script objects from a pooled allocator; CPU
 counters for hordes

Lexicon slaughter maps with Brutal Doom ran 16-25 ms tics with ~2000
actors. A repeatable horde (150 Brutal imps, local test mod) showed where:
spawning ~50 actors per tic (the imps' hitbox helpers) cost 2.5 ms, almost
all of it newlib's malloc, ~47 us per ~1.6 KB object. PClass::CreateNew and
the GC sweep now use NXObj_Alloc/NXObj_Free: free lists per 16-byte size
class carved from 128 KB slabs (blocks kept for reuse, other pointers go to
M_Free). Horde tic in Ryujinx: 7.2 -> 4.5 ms; spawning 2.5 -> 0.34 ms.

perf.log per tic: collision (position checks, actors tested), sight checks,
actors spawned with create/link/place/BeginPlay, object creation parts, and
the game thread's malloc/free per frame (linker --wrap, handle-checked).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
